<string_table>
	<string id="ui_mcm_menu_fotz">
		<text>Factions of the Zone</text>
	</string>
	<string id="ui_mcm_fotz_politics">
		<text>Factions change their relations</text>
	</string>
	<string id="ui_mcm_fotz_politics_desc">
		<text>Once a game day, kills, ground taken and fronts move the relations between factions, and wars, truces and alliances follow. Turned off, every faction goes back to the relations the game gave it.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="ui_mcm_fotz_territory">
		<text>Squads lean toward winning fronts</text>
	</string>
	<string id="ui_mcm_fotz_territory_desc">
		<text>A faction sends its squads toward ground its enemies hold where it outnumbers them on that level, and less often where it is outnumbered. Only a bias in the game's own choice of where squads go: no orders, no new squads. Off in Warfare mode, which runs the squads itself.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="ui_mcm_fotz_news">
		<text>News on the PDA</text>
	</string>
	<string id="ui_mcm_fotz_news_desc">
		<text>Factions announce wars, truces and alliances on the PDA. With Everything, they also report the ground they take.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="ui_mcm_lst_fotz_news_off">
		<text>Off</text>
	</string>
	<string id="ui_mcm_lst_fotz_news_events">
		<text>Wars, truces and alliances</text>
	</string>
	<string id="ui_mcm_lst_fotz_news_all">
		<text>Everything</text>
	</string>
	<string id="ui_mcm_fotz_census">
		<text>Keep a census</text>
	</string>
	<string id="ui_mcm_fotz_census_desc">
		<text>Once a game day, and once after each load, count every faction's squads and the ground they hold, and write it to fotz_census.jsonl in the game's appdata folder. It changes nothing in the game.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="ui_mcm_fotz_about">
		<text>Relations change only between factions the base game lets change, within lore limits. Factions of the Zone steps aside while the base game's dynamic relations, Fluid Relations, Dynamic Faction Relations Customizer, or Warfare mode handle relations.</text>
	</string>
